<a href=3D"https://www.reuters.com/business/media-telecom/verizon-signs-opt=
ical-fiber-deal-with-corning-expand-broadband-support-ai-growth-2026-09-08/=
">https://www.reuters.com/business/media-telecom/verizon-signs-optical-fibe=
r-deal-with-corning-expand-broadband-support-ai-growth-2026-09-08/</a><br>
<a href=3D"https://introl.com/uk/blog/germanium-chokepoint-china-fiber-opti=
c-supply-chain-2026">https://introl.com/uk/blog/germanium-chokepoint-china-=
fiber-optic-supply-chain-2026</a></p>
<ol>
<li>EMBEDDED-UTILITY TOLL ROADS =E2=80=94 gases are capacity rights, not co=
mmodities</li>
</ol>
<p>Air Liquide=E2=80=99s April 2026 decision to invest =E2=82=AC200M in two=
 Japanese ultra-high-purity gas units under a long-term semiconductor custo=
mer agreement illustrates a useful distinction: advanced fabs do not simply=
 buy commodity nitrogen/argon/oxygen. They rely on qualified, site-specific=
, continuously available gas infrastructure that is often financed and oper=
ated under long-term contracts.</p>
<p>Air Products likewise disclosed new Samsung wins involving owned/operate=
d production facilities and bulk specialty-gas systems.</p>
<p>The hidden asset is therefore not gas itself but embedded qualified util=
ity capacity sitting physically beside a fab.</p>
<p>New variable: utility_lock_in =3D qualification_cost =C3=97 switching_do=
wntime =C3=97 onsite_asset_specificity =C3=97 contract_duration.</p>
<p>This has lower equity convexity in Air Liquide/Air Products because they=
 are enormous diversified businesses. Better rabbit hole: Japanese specialt=
y-gas producers such as Kanto Denka Kogyo, Nippon Sanso, Resonac and smalle=
r purifier/abatement suppliers.</p>
<p>Falsifiers: fabs aggressively insource gases; commoditization/supplier c=
ompetition removes pricing power; semiconductor capacity additions underper=
form announced plans.</p>
