<ol>
<li>PURE-MATERIAL READINESS =E2=80=94 Toyo Gosei shows a different kind of =
qualification debt</li>
</ol>
<p>Toyo Gosei (TSE:4970) has expanded cutting-edge photosensitive-material =
capacity to 1.8x and semiconductor high-purity-solvent shipping capacity to=
 ~3x. Management explicitly says semiconductor innovation is now moving so =
quickly that when customers ask for a new material there is no longer time =
to develop the underlying technology from scratch; capacity and R&amp;D mus=
t exist in advance.</p>
<p>That is direct evidence for our qualification-debt thesis: suppliers mus=
t spend before demand is contractually certain because customer innovation =
cycles are shorter than chemical qualification/build cycles.</p>
<p>The stock is small (~=C2=A584B market cap) but has roughly doubled in va=
lue over the past year and remains operationally volatile; recent TTM earni=
ngs were negative despite long-term AI-linked materials demand.</p>
<p>New signal: prequalification_capex_ratio =3D capacity/R&amp;D committed =
before customer production qualification divided by current revenue. High v=
alues can identify both convex future winners and dangerous stranded-capita=
l situations.</p>
<p>Falsifiers: qualification slips, utilization remains low, customer archi=
tectures change before the new lines fill, or fixed-cost absorption overwhe=
lms volume growth.</p>
